Report: Integer single-bit operations and generic slice routing, with exact failure cases
27 claims; 0 removal(s).
  limitations: "Only twenty-four primitive single-bit methods, twelve width constants and three callback-conditional slice bodies are established. Primitive and slice get_bits/set_bits range methods remain unproved. A separately Kani-checked example shows signed range behavior differs from ordinary masked updates: 112_i8.set_bits(0..4,1) yields 1, changing high bits outside the range; the unsigned example yields 113. The verified single-bit methods are unaffected. Generic callback side effects, failure/divergence outside the stated contracts, other targets and release extraction are not established. No generic Rust size_of property, panic text or unwinding-state guarantee is claimed." -> "Only twenty-four primitive single-bit methods, twelve width constants and three callback-conditional slice bodies are established. Primitive and slice get_bits/set_bits range methods remain unproved. A separately Kani-checked example shows signed range behavior differs from ordinary masked updates: 112_i8.set_bits(0..4,1) yields 1, changing high bits outside the range; the unsigned example yields 113. The verified single-bit methods are unaffected. Generic callback side effects, failure/divergence outside the stated contracts, other targets and release extraction are not established. No generic Rust size_of property, panic text or unwinding-state guarantee is claimed. Signed-range diagnostic evidence: https://github.com/nyuichi/rust-crate-proofs/tree/57c4d16e1184f84353db90589bc3cb601f89cb85/batches/2026-11-05-full-public-api/diagnostics/bit-field-signed-range"
